<comment datatype='string'>The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-12262&quot;&gt;paaG&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-198931&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Pseudomonas&lt;/i&gt; sp. &lt;i&gt;Y2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has been cloned and expressed in &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-562&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as a His-fusion protein. The recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity, and shown to catalyze the reversible isomerization of &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD0-2362&quot;&gt;2-(1,2-epoxy-1,2-dihydrophenyl)acetyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt; to another product. 
&lt;sup&gt;13&lt;/sup&gt;C-NMR spectroscopy identified this isomer as an unusual unsaturated, oxygen-containing, seven-member heterocyclic enol ether, namely 2-oxepin-2(3H)-ylideneacetyl-CoA (&lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD0-2363&quot;&gt;2-oxepin-2(3H)-ylideneacetyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt;).</comment>
